Subject: [PATCH] ipa: libipa: camera_sensor_helper: add imx681

Add a CameraSensorHelper for the Sony IMX681 (Surface Pro 11 front camera). The
analogue gain is the Sony reciprocal law the Windows tuning data states
(code = 512 - 512 / gain, codes 0 to 479, 1.0x to 15.5x), expressed in the
existing AnalogueGainLinear model as (0 * code + 512) / (-1 * code + 512), the same
form as the imx219 helper. The law is per Windows analysis, not measured on the
device (hardware/cameras/evidence/2026-10-31-bayer-units-gain-crosscheck.md).

No black level is set: its scale is not established (quality-parity U6), the tuning
file carries it. Without the helper libcamera logs "Failed to create camera sensor
helper for imx681" and uses the control value as the gain.

Applies after libcamera-sp11.patch on libcamera v0.7.2 (and on a clean v0.7.2,
the context is unrelated to that patch).

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
---
diff --git a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
index 413d7c8..3367f7f 100644
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -654,6 +654,22 @@ public:
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx678", CameraSensorHelperImx678)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperImx681 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperImx681()
+	{
+		/*
+		 * Sony reciprocal analogue gain, from the Windows tuning data:
+		 * code = 512 - 512 / gain, so gain = 512 / (512 - code), with
+		 * codes 0..479 (1.0x to 15.5x). No black level: its scale is
+		 * not established, the tuning file provides it.
+		 */
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 0, 512, -1, 512 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx681", CameraSensorHelperImx681)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperImx708 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
